      "description": "Create a background monitor that watches for a condition and settles when it becomes true. Evaluation happens inside the plugin, so never write your own sleep/poll loop. Set wait_timeout_seconds to block until it settles, which is the usual case; omit it to get a monitor id back immediately and pause later with monitor_wait. Use this for anything long-running: cluster jobs, builds, deploys, downloads, servers coming up. Installed condition types: command, file, log.",
